<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">973–1024</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Saint Henry</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry II, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>, was the last Ottonian ruler, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> from 1002 and emperor from 1014. He defeated the Italian rival king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea">Arduin of Ivrea</a> and fought long wars with Bolesław I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, ended by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-bautzen">Peace of Bautzen</a> in 1018. A church reformer, he restored the bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merseburg">Merseburg</a> and founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bamberg">Bamberg</a>, and was later canonised.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-ii-holy-roman-emperor.jpg" alt="Henry II, Holy Roman Emperor" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kronung_Heinrich_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
